    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529-a8">

                <pb facs="0731" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg637"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2 to inclosure 2 in No.
                        517.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commandant to Mr.
                            Hyatt.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Marine Department and Office of the Captain of the Port of Santiago
                                de Cuba</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santiago de
                            Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-05-14"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 14, 1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Consul of the United
                        States:</hi></p>
                <p>His excellency the comandante general de marina del apostadero de la Habana
                    (general commandant of marine department at Habana) in a cablegram of yesterday
                    says to me the following: “You can communicate to the American consul that the
                        <pb facs="0732" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/> cause against Skiller will pass to
                    ordinary jurisdiction as soon as it arrives by first mail.” Which I have the
                    honor to notify you for your knowledge and satisfaction.</p>
                <p>God keep you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel be Eliza.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
